# shell: desktop
# mount: /devices/board1
# board: only
# A window of the board's own: its process opens it by title and size
# and draws it as a list of the desktop's controls, a few hundred bytes
# over the same console the shell uses.  A press on its button goes back
# over that line as an event, and the process redraws the count.  This
# needs a board on the cable, so it runs only with one.
wait 30
note the board's window is on the desktop, beside its form
expect-windows 3
click 430 227
wait 20
expect-title Board window
expect-narrate Pressed 1 time
note the window also carries tabs and a scrollbar, said as themselves
expect-narrate tabs
expect-narrate scrollbar
note a second press, past the double-click interval, counts again
wait 40
click 445 230
wait 20
expect-narrate Pressed 2 times
shot /tmp/trk_boarddraw.png
quit
